Source: wash
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: wash
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adduser,
         libcap2-bin
Recommends: ca-certificates
Description: lightweight remote-admin desktop environment
 wash is a transport-only router and a small family of web-component
 apps that present a Windows/GNOME/macOS-style desktop over HTTP/WS.
 Designed for maintaining Linux machines over the network without
 needing SSH plus a stack of text-only tools.
 .
 This package installs the wash-* binaries to /usr/bin/. wash-router
 is the entry point; per-user multi-session support (wash-login) is
 planned but not yet shipped.

Package: wash-display
Architecture: amd64 arm64
# Opt-in, mirroring rpm's `%bcond_with display` and alpine's WASH_DISPLAY=1:
# wash-display is a C++/CMake build (wlroots/codec stack) NOT produced by the
# default `build.sh --standalone`, so populating it unconditionally aborts
# dh_install ("missing files: out/wash-display"). Gate the whole binary
# package behind a build profile — without `DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=pkg.wash.display`
# dpkg-buildpackage skips it, and the main wash package builds clean.
Build-Profiles: <pkg.wash.display>
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         wash (= ${binary:Version}),
         xwayland
Description: native X/Wayland app surfaces for wash
 wash-display runs native Linux GUI apps (Wayland and X11 via Xwayland)
 as first-class wash windows: each app surface is captured, encoded, and
 streamed to the browser shell, with input and clipboard bridged back.
 .
 Split from the main wash package because it links the compositor stack
 (wlroots) and a media/transport stack the pure-Go core deliberately
 avoids. Install only on hosts that serve native GUI apps.
